# ML-KEM keys, encapsulations and certificates from OpenSSL.
#
# Generated by scripts/capture_mlkem.py. Do not edit: every value
# here is OpenSSL's, and the tests that read it need no OpenSSL.
#
# OpenSSL 3.5.4 30 Sep 2025 (Library: OpenSSL 3.5.4 30 Sep 2025)
#
# PEM bodies are written as one line of base64. `[key]` holds one
# key per parameter set in the three forms of RFC 9935 section 6;
# `[encapsulation]` is `pkeyutl -encap` to that key's public half;
# `[certificate]` is an ML-KEM certificate and the ML-DSA CA that
# issued it.
#
# Counts, asserted by the test that reads this:
#   key                      3
#   encapsulation            9
#   certificate              3

